{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RcubhmkSfPWZ9sp2PfsL1K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation: make claude model configurable\n2\t\n3\tid: measure\n4\tdeveloper: @developer\n5\tdate: 2026-08-29\n6\t\n7\t## Summary\n8\t\n9\tClaude Code profiles can now be given a model override the same way OpenCode\n10\tprofiles already could. `config.Profile.ModelEnv`/`ModelDefault` are no\n11\tlonger opencode-only: `session.ResolveProfile` resolves a new\n12\t`ProfileInfo.ClaudeModel` field for claude-code profiles (mirroring\n13\t`OpenCodeModel`), and both the docker session path and `mg host` forward it\n14\tto the `claude` CLI as a real `--model <value>` argv flag (verified accepted\n15\tby the installed CLI via `claude --help`). `mg profiles add` now offers an\n16\toptional model prompt for claude-code profiles, and `mg setup <profile>`\n17\tprompts for it too. `claude-pro`'s `ModelDefault` — previously the\n18\tdisplay-only sentinel string `\"(Claude Code default)\"` — is now empty, with\n19\tthat sentinel moved into `cmd/mg/profiles.go`'s `profileModel()` display\n20\tlogic, so `claude-pro`'s own behavior (no override, CLI's own default) is\n21\tunchanged.\n22\t\n23\t## Changes\n24\t\n25\tTASK-1: `internal/config/config.go` — generalized the `ModelEnv`/\n26\t`ModelDefault` doc comments to cover claude-code profiles, and changed the\n27\tbuilt-in `claude-pro` profile's `ModelDefault` from `\"(Claude Code default)\"`\n28\tto unset (no `ModelEnv`/`ModelDefault` at all), since that sentinel string\n29\tmust never be forwarded to the CLI as a literal `--model` value.\n30\t\n31\tTASK-2: `internal/session/session.go` — added `ProfileInfo.ClaudeModel`,\n32\tpopulated in `ResolveProfile` for `claude-code`-tool profiles via\n33\t`envDefault(p.ModelEnv, p.ModelDefault)`, mirroring the existing\n34\t`OpenCodeModel` resolution. Added `session_test.go` coverage: a user-defined\n35\tclaude profile with an env override, one falling back to its stored default,\n36\tand `claude-pro` resolving to `\"\"`.\n37\t\n38\tTASK-3: `internal/session/docker.go` — `BuildDockerInvocation` now appends\n39\t`--model <ClaudeModel>` to the container command's argv (after `--agent`,\n40\tbefore the prompt/passthrough args) when the resolved profile is\n41\t`claude-code` with a non-empty `ClaudeModel`. Verified `claude --help` lists\n42\t`--model` as an accepted flag on the installed CLI. Added `docker_test.go`\n43\tcoverage for both the flag-present and no-model (`claude-pro`) cases,\n44\tincluding flag position relative to `--agent`.\n45\t\n46\tTASK-4: `internal/session/host.go` — extended `BuildHostInvocation`'s\n47\t`modelArgs` construction to also cover `claude-code` profiles with a\n48\tnon-empty `ClaudeModel`, using the exact same `--model` flag mechanism\n49\talready used for opencode's host path. Added `host_test.go` coverage\n50\tmirroring the existing opencode model tests.\n51\t\n52\tTASK-5: `cmd/mg/profiles.go` — the `mg profiles add` wizard now prompts for\n53\ta model `.env` key and default when the chosen tool is `claude-code`,\n54\tmirroring the opencode prompt but optional (leaving both blank is valid,\n55\tmatching `claude-pro`'s own shape). `profileModel()` (the table/picker's\n56\tmodel column) now shows `\"(Claude Code default)\"` when the effective\n57\tresolved value is empty and the profile's tool is `claude-code`, rather than\n58\treading that string out of `ModelDefault`. Added `profiles_test.go` coverage\n59\tfor both the model-blank and model-set add-wizard paths.\n60\t\n61\tTASK-6: `cmd/mg/setup.go` — `setupClaudePro` now takes the profile's\n62\t`config.Profile` and, after its existing OAuth-credential flow, calls a new\n63\t`setupClaudeModel` — an optional model prompt using `p.ModelEnv`/\n64\t`p.ModelDefault`, skipped entirely when a profile defines neither (which is\n65\t`claude-pro`'s own case, so its wizard output is byte-identical to before).\n66\tAdded `setup_test.go` coverage for a user-defined claude profile's model\n67\tprompt and confirmed `claude-pro`'s wizard shows no model prompt.\n68\t\n69\tTASK-7: `internal/config/config_test.go` — updated the pinned\n70\t`TestBuiltInProfilesCarryAuthAndModelMetadata` assertion for `claude-pro`'s\n71\t`ModelDefault` to `\"\"`. Grepped the whole repo for the literal string\n72\t`\"(Claude Code default)\"`: every remaining occurrence is in\n73\t`cmd/mg/profiles.go`'s `profileModel()` (the new display-only path) or its\n74\taccompanying doc comments/tests — none left in a data field.\n75\t\n76\tTASK-8: `README.md`'s `mg host` bullet described model forwarding as an\n77\tOpenCode-only mechanism (\"**OpenCode model.**\"); reworded to\n78\t\"**Model.**\" and extended to mention a claude-code profile's own model is\n79\tforwarded the same way via claude's `--model` flag. Also fixed the matching\n80\tdoc comment on `profilesAdd` in `cmd/mg/profiles.go`, which described the\n81\tmodel prompt as opencode-only. No other doc files (`docs/AGENTS.md`,\n82\t`AGENTS.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`, `agents/*.md`) contained\n83\twording that was actually wrong after TASK-5/TASK-6 — none of them claimed\n84\tmodel configuration was opencode-specific, so none were touched, per the\n85\ttask's scope boundary against unrelated rewrites.\n86\t\n87\t## Known issues / follow-ups\n88\t\n89\t- `setupClaudePro`'s wizard prose and title (\"claude-pro — Claude Code,\n90\t  billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription...\") are still specific to\n91\t  `claude-pro`'s own wording even when run for a user-defined claude-code\n92\t  profile, and it still prompts the four fixed `CLAUDE_*` OAuth keys\n93\t  regardless of the profile's own `AuthKeys`. Both are pre-existing gaps\n94\t  called out as out of scope in tasks.md's design notes; only the new model\n95\t  prompt block was added on top.\n96\t- `claude --model <value>`'s exact accepted value shapes were spot-checked\n97\t  via `claude --help` (which documents both short aliases like `sonnet`/\n98\t  `opus` and full model ids) but not exhaustively tested against every value\n99\t  shape at runtime — no environment with real Claude Code credentials was\n100\t  available in this session to launch an actual container/host session.\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef648619-dfbf-4430-a8e3-47acb5e23923","uuid":"acbd0f69-1136-4f1a-b397-5cb88839d6ab","timestamp":"2026-08-29T09:11:19.903Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/measure_make-claude-model-configurable/implementation.md","content":"# Implementation: make claude model configurable\n\nid: measure\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Summary\n\nClaude Code profiles can now be given a model override the same way OpenCode\nprofiles already could. `config.Profile.ModelEnv`/`ModelDefault` are no\nlonger opencode-only: `session.ResolveProfile` resolves a new\n`ProfileInfo.ClaudeModel` field for claude-code profiles (mirroring\n`OpenCodeModel`), and both the docker session path and `mg host` forward it\nto the `claude` CLI as a real `--model <value>` argv flag (verified accepted\nby the installed CLI via `claude --help`). `mg profiles add` now offers an\noptional model prompt for claude-code profiles, and `mg setup <profile>`\nprompts for it too. `claude-pro`'s `ModelDefault` — previously the\ndisplay-only sentinel string `\"(Claude Code default)\"` — is now empty, with\nthat sentinel moved into `cmd/mg/profiles.go`'s `profileModel()` display\nlogic, so `claude-pro`'s own behavior (no override, CLI's own default) is\nunchanged.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `internal/config/config.go` — generalized the `ModelEnv`/\n`ModelDefault` doc comments to cover claude-code profiles, and changed the\nbuilt-in `claude-pro` profile's `ModelDefault` from `\"(Claude Code default)\"`\nto unset (no `ModelEnv`/`ModelDefault` at all), since that sentinel string\nmust never be forwarded to the CLI as a literal `--model` value.\n\nTASK-2: `internal/session/session.go` — added `ProfileInfo.ClaudeModel`,\npopulated in `ResolveProfile` for `claude-code`-tool profiles via\n`envDefault(p.ModelEnv, p.ModelDefault)`, mirroring the existing\n`OpenCodeModel` resolution. Added `session_test.go` coverage: a user-defined\nclaude profile with an env override, one falling back to its stored default,\nand `claude-pro` resolving to `\"\"`.\n\nTASK-3: `internal/session/docker.go` — `BuildDockerInvocation` now appends\n`--model <ClaudeModel>` to the container command's argv (after `--agent`,\nbefore the prompt/passthrough args) when the resolved profile is\n`claude-code` with a non-empty `ClaudeModel`. Verified `claude --help` lists\n`--model` as an accepted flag on the installed CLI. Added `docker_test.go`\ncoverage for both the flag-present and no-model (`claude-pro`) cases,\nincluding flag position relative to `--agent`.\n\nTASK-4: `internal/session/host.go` — extended `BuildHostInvocation`'s\n`modelArgs` construction to also cover `claude-code` profiles with a\nnon-empty `ClaudeModel`, using the exact same `--model` flag mechanism\nalready used for opencode's host path. Added `host_test.go` coverage\nmirroring the existing opencode model tests.\n\nTASK-5: `cmd/mg/profiles.go` — the `mg profiles add` wizard now prompts for\na model `.env` key and default when the chosen tool is `claude-code`,\nmirroring the opencode prompt but optional (leaving both blank is valid,\nmatching `claude-pro`'s own shape). `profileModel()` (the table/picker's\nmodel column) now shows `\"(Claude Code default)\"` when the effective\nresolved value is empty and the profile's tool is `claude-code`, rather than\nreading that string out of `ModelDefault`. Added `profiles_test.go` coverage\nfor both the model-blank and model-set add-wizard paths.\n\nTASK-6: `cmd/mg/setup.go` — `setupClaudePro` now takes the profile's\n`config.Profile` and, after its existing OAuth-credential flow, calls a new\n`setupClaudeModel` — an optional model prompt using `p.ModelEnv`/\n`p.ModelDefault`, skipped entirely when a profile defines neither (which is\n`claude-pro`'s own case, so its wizard output is byte-identical to before).\nAdded `setup_test.go` coverage for a user-defined claude profile's model\nprompt and confirmed `claude-pro`'s wizard shows no model prompt.\n\nTASK-7: `internal/config/config_test.go` — updated the pinned\n`TestBuiltInProfilesCarryAuthAndModelMetadata` assertion for `claude-pro`'s\n`ModelDefault` to `\"\"`. Grepped the whole repo for the literal string\n`\"(Claude Code default)\"`: every remaining occurrence is in\n`cmd/mg/profiles.go`'s `profileModel()` (the new display-only path) or its\naccompanying doc comments/tests — none left in a data field.\n\nTASK-8: `README.md`'s `mg host` bullet described model forwarding as an\nOpenCode-only mechanism (\"**OpenCode model.**\"); reworded to\n\"**Model.**\" and extended to mention a claude-code profile's own model is\nforwarded the same way via claude's `--model` flag. Also fixed the matching\ndoc comment on `profilesAdd` in `cmd/mg/profiles.go`, which described the\nmodel prompt as opencode-only. No other doc files (`docs/AGENTS.md`,\n`AGENTS.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`, `agents/*.md`) contained\nwording that was actually wrong after TASK-5/TASK-6 — none of them claimed\nmodel configuration was opencode-specific, so none were touched, per the\ntask's scope boundary against unrelated rewrites.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- `setupClaudePro`'s wizard prose and title (\"claude-pro — Claude Code,\n  billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription...\") are still specific to\n  `claude-pro`'s own wording even when run for a user-defined claude-code\n  profile, and it still prompts the four fixed `CLAUDE_*` OAuth keys\n  regardless of the profile's own `AuthKeys`. Both are pre-existing gaps\n  called out as out of scope in tasks.md's design notes; only the new model\n  prompt block was added on top.\n- `claude --model <value>`'s exact accepted value shapes were spot-checked\n  via `claude --help` (which documents both short aliases like `sonnet`/\n  `opus` and full model ids) but not exhaustively tested against every value\n  shape at runtime — no environment with real Claude Code credentials was\n  available in this session to launch an actual container/host session.\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
